# The harness binaries. measure.sh builds them into a mktemp directory OUTSIDE
# the checkout on purpose — building inside the measured container would charge
# the Go compiler's memory to the cgroup M(x) reads — but a bare
# `go build ./cmd/memsrv` run by hand while diagnosing writes an 18 MB artifact
# here, and one did. The repository-root list names the three example binaries
# and nothing under test/.
/memsrv
/memdrv
/memstat
/memdiag
